  <p>Key structural shifts include the OPEC embargo (1973), the Iranian Revolution (1979), the 1986 price collapse, the 2008 supercycle peak and crash, the 2014 shale-driven decline, and the COVID-19 demand shock (2020). The overall standard deviation of <strong>${overall_std:.2f}</strong> underscores the inherently volatile nature of crude oil pricing.</p>

